adjudication.rationale:
In `EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents`, the code now iterates `for (const destination of event.destinationCalendar)`. For each `destination` **without** `credentialId`, it executes the `else` branch:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(
  (c) => c.type === destination.integration
);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

Because this fan-out happens *inside the per-destination loop* and does not use any property unique to that destination (it ignores `destination.externalId` here), two destination entries that share the same `integration` and lack `credentialId` will cause the same set of credentials to be used multiple times, creating duplicate calendar events for the same booking. This duplication behavior is directly verifiable from the diff.
